                        ],
                        "form": "die Einsilbigkeit"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a57c6467-3b3e-378a-822d-321d8d0362f6",
                        "entry_id": "4b0a976c-e610-3779-8506-ff7890b9638a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Eigenschaft, aus genau einer Silbe zu bestehen"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8b7b12fb-b205-4bd9-a713-c2818ba9c02d",
                                "sense_id": "a57c6467-3b3e-378a-822d-321d8d0362f6",
                                "text": "„Was shit betrifft, ist dieses Wort möglicherweise drastischer als seine deutsche Entsprechung, und in seiner Einsilbigkeit mit dem kurzen Vokal und dem harten konsonantischen Ausgang ist es wohl auch expressiver und vielleicht schon deshalb schärfer (…).“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8f187b3e-f3dc-3c55-8648-72b48fd2fbc7",
                        "entry_id": "4b0a976c-e610-3779-8506-ff7890b9638a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Eigenschaft, sich auf möglichst kurze Äußerungen zu beschränken"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ff457d9d-1abb-4c6c-9e62-7a7157b5f4aa",
                                "sense_id": "8f187b3e-f3dc-3c55-8648-72b48fd2fbc7",
                                "text": "Kurt war für seine kurzen, treffenden Kommentare bekannt, für seine Einsilbigkeit, die so manchen Gesprächspartner reizte."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f9ee3a46-f596-4a19-8410-8ae5bf6485fd",
                                "sense_id": "8f187b3e-f3dc-3c55-8648-72b48fd2fbc7",
                                "text": "„Wortkargheit ist indes nicht nur verzögerte, langsame Sprechweise und Einsilbigkeit, sondern es ist zuweilen auch die Kunst, mit wenig Worten viel zu sagen.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "38ed972a-19b1-43fa-afff-a512ff9ee709",
                                "sense_id": "8f187b3e-f3dc-3c55-8648-72b48fd2fbc7",
                                "text": "„Meine bisherige Einsilbigkeit wich dem gewandten Charme eines Chesterfield oder dem gottlosen Zynismus eines Rochester.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "393dc64d-7f49-4384-860d-b114ae6e9273",
                        "source_entry_id": "4b0a976c-e610-3779-8506-ff7890b9638a",
                        "source_sense_id": "a57c6467-3b3e-378a-822d-321d8d0362f6",
                        "source_sense_description": "Eigenschaft, aus genau einer Silbe zu bestehen",
                        "target_lang_word": "taciturnity",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "taciturnity",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5e4c3165-70ff-3d71-8870-283a91bb4663",
                                        "entry_id": "6384772e-f091-31bc-8532-bccdace2d9d7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The trait of being taciturn."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d49795b9-7b66-4fba-bf90-2322cdff9bff",
                                                "sense_id": "5e4c3165-70ff-3d71-8870-283a91bb4663",
                                                "text": "Humphries broke out more freely into speech than he had done before, for his usual characteristic was that of taciturnity."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "62eae02b-1cb7-4f6d-a6b8-ff26b138324c",
                                                "sense_id": "5e4c3165-70ff-3d71-8870-283a91bb4663",
                                                "text": "Gernois’ cordiality was short-lived. No sooner had they ridden out of sight of Captain Gerard and his men than he lapsed once more into his accustomed taciturnity."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8479b40c-3207-470c-87a6-40823abb4ba6",
                                                "sense_id": "5e4c3165-70ff-3d71-8870-283a91bb4663",
                                                "text": "\"[…]and as Mr. H., with his long purse and his willingness to receive hints, is no bad card in the game, he has been brought up to Abbotsford for a week; his taciturnity has long ago fled, and he is one of the most loquacious Borderers going. […]\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd12764a-3f55-429b-b110-33c179f185b5",
                                                "sense_id": "5e4c3165-70ff-3d71-8870-283a91bb4663",
                                                "text": "Once he is back on the bench, will Justice Thomas revert to his usual taciturnity?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "90393d21-25b6-3a0e-a4d1-ff5b8b7232ad",
                                        "entry_id": "6384772e-f091-31bc-8532-bccdace2d9d7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Failure to assert a legal right in a way that implies that it is being given up."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Scotland",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
